<title>UK: Epicore shares admitted to AIM.</title>
<headline>Epicore shares admitted to AIM.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Not a single trade was registered in Canada's Epicore Networks shares, which made their debut on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Monday.</p>
<p>At 1330 GMT, the shares were marked up at 55p, ahead of their December 27 close of C$1.10, or about 48p, on the Alberta Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Henderson Crosthwaite acted as broker and advisor to the company, which uses natural microbes and enzymes to make products used in various sectors including fish farming.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
